      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T03:42:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder: should we just do this regardless of whether the new network has TRANSPORT_PRIMARY or not? If the radio can\u0027t timeshare, maybe skipping the linger timer is the right thing to do regardless of whether the new network is TRANSPORT_PRIMARY or not?\n\nNot sure when this might actually happen though. What other factors than TRANSPORT_PRIMARY might cause such a switch? Perhaps lack of validation on a DS-DA device when both networks are up? Or...?\n\nI guess checking for TRANSPORT_PRIMARY is safest here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8100,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 8100,
        "endChar": 94
      },
      "revId": "a5c76243af0e0d298db88b3e1e23f760ac9fd2e9",
