      "writtenOn": "2021-09-17T09:48:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Originally I added this to restrict usage of this more closely to the use case we know about, but didn\u0027t think too hard about it as it was just a proof of concept.\n\nThe control can come here without the new network being primary in a few cases.\n- If the old network becomes unvalidated. This kind of requires it\u0027s a DSDA device with both networks connected at the same time. In that case I think strictly it\u0027s good to linger the request, because the reasons that may lead a mobile network to become unvalidated might not imply carrier apps lose access to their internal network.\n- If the old network is now exiting. I don\u0027t think it happens today, but a typical use case would be that the device is moving out of CBRS range. This also kind of implies this was a DSDA device... unless macro is 3G and it\u0027s a different radio ?\n\nI don\u0027t think it matters much really, because both of these cases would deal reasonably well with either behavior, but it does serve to document the intent a little bit and to reduce the surface for \"creative\" uses.\n\nKept.",
      "parentUuid": "da0f1e85_bef3f352",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 8100,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 8100,
        "endChar": 94
